    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) – picture of a ram's head. See also the original version of 沈.\nFrom Proto-Sino-Tibetan *jaŋ (“sheep”). Cognate with Tibetan གཡང་དཀར (g.yang dkar), Tangut 𗂽 (*ꞏjij², “sheep”), and Northern Tujia zo³⁵ (“goat; sheep”)."
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Orthographic borrowing from translingual ¥. Perhaps influenced by 大洋 (dàyáng)."
    }
  ],
